From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:24:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] feature: cancel the autosuspend countdown when the user
 is active again

The inactivity monitor stops once it has warned about an imminent
autosuspend, so nothing watches for the user coming back. Moving the mouse
or pressing a key -- which is exactly what someone does when the screen
wakes and the countdown appears -- did nothing, and the suspend fired unless
they reached the Cancel button in time.

autodimm already solved "the user is active again": it polls the X idle time
and re-brightens the display. Move that poll -- startCheckForActivity(), the
UserIsActiveAgain() signal and the polling slot -- down into the shared
inactivity base class so autosuspend gets it too, and have the countdown
subscribe: on activity it closes the dialog, which (being WDestructiveClose)
reports time remaining and so routes to the cancel path, stopping the
suspend and restarting monitoring exactly as the Cancel button does.

Signed-off-by: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
